Given sides of parallelogram,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\vec{a}=\hat{i}+\hat{k} \\
\vec{b}=2 \hat{i}+\hat{j}+\hat{k}
\end{array}
\]<br>So, area is given by \( |\vec{a} \times \vec{b}| \)<br>\[
\left|\begin{array}{lll}
\hat{i} & \hat{j} & \hat{k} \\
1 & 0 & 1 \\
2 & 1 & 1
\end{array}\right|=-\hat{i}+\hat{j}+\hat{k}
\]<br>Therefore, area of parallelogram, is \( \sqrt{1+1+1}=\sqrt{3} \)

Given that, events \( A \) and \( B \) are independent events,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
P(A)=\frac{2}{3} \text { and } P(B)=\frac{2}{7} \\
P(A \cap B)=P(A) \cdot P(B) \\
=[1-P(A)][1-P(B)] \\
=\left(1-\frac{2}{3}\right)\left(1-\frac{2}{7}\right) \\
=\frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{5}{7}=\frac{5}{21}
\end{array}
\]

Given equation,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\frac{x-2}{1}=\frac{y-3}{1}=\frac{z-4}{-K} \rightarrow(1) \\
\frac{x-1}{K}=\frac{y-4}{2}=\frac{z-5}{1} \rightarrow(2)
\end{array}
\]<br>For co-planarity, we have<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\left|\begin{array}{ccc}
x_{2}-x_{1} & y_{2}-y_{2} & z_{2}-z_{1} \\
a_{1} & b_{1} & c_{1} \\
a_{2} & b_{2} & c_{2}
