\Rightarrow\left|\begin{array}{cccc}
1 & 1 & 1 & -K \\
K & 2 & 1 & =0
\end{array}\right|=0
\end{array}
\]

Given differential equation is,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\frac{d y}{d x}+\frac{y}{x}=3 x \rightarrow(1) \\
\Rightarrow x \frac{d y}{d x}+y=3 x^{2} \\
\Rightarrow \frac{d}{d x}(x y)=3 x^{2} \rightarrow(2)
\end{array}
\]<br>On integrating, we get;<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
x y=x^{3}+c \\
\Rightarrow y=\frac{x^{3}+c}{x}
\end{array}
\]<br>After integrating equation (2), we have<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
x y=x^{3}-c \\
\Rightarrow y=x^{2}-\frac{C}{x}
\end{array}
\]

